(lang dune 3.21)

; An executable records where the compiler that linked it keeps the standard
; library, and a toplevel, such as quill's kernel or mdx's generator, loads it
; from there. dune builds the compiler inside _build, so that place differs
; between trees, while dune's shared cache keys a link by a command that names
; the compiler relative to _build. A tree then restored another tree's
; executables with their path, and they failed once that tree was removed.
; Every link passes the path the linker would record as an argument, which the
; cache key holds. dune-workspace.tsan repeats it.

(env
 (_
  (link_flags
   (:standard
    -set-runtime-default
    standard_library_default=%{ocaml-config:standard_library_default}))))
